---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../content';
import { APPS, SEGMENTS, USE_CASES } from '../content';
const path = '/';
const title = 'Shopify abandoned cart app selection';
const desc = 'Compare recovery requirements, catalog constraints and operating effort before replacing your workflow.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/guides">Explore related guides</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Shopify abandoned cart app selection</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Compare recovery requirements, catalog constraints and operating effort before replacing your workflow.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Start with the missing capability</h2>
<p>If shoppers cannot complete payment, investigate checkout first. If messages continue after purchase, investigate event delivery and queue ownership. If the offer is expensive, investigate contribution and stacking. Use the <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">cart workflow guide</a> to define enrollment, transitions and exits before asking vendors for a demonstration.</p>
<h2>Build a shortlist from evidence</h2>
<p>Ask each candidate to show one of your actual basket types, its event source, permission record, selected variants, purchase exit and exclusion log. Include the native Shopify workflow in the comparison rather than assuming a paid replacement is necessary. Sequenzy can be evaluated alongside other candidates; inclusion here is not an integration claim, ranking or tested recommendation.</p>
<h2>Browse the app catalog</h2>
<p>The directory keeps routes to product research, including historical entries that may require a migration decision. Check current availability and supplier documentation before shortlisting. Names and catalog order do not imply current feature coverage or scores.</p>
<h2>Catalog entries</h2>
<p>{APPS.map(app => <a class="link mr-4 inline-block mb-3" href={app.slug === 'sequenzy' ? '/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo' : `/alternatives/${app.slug}-alternative`}>{app.name}</a>)}</p>
<h2>Select the store constraint</h2>
<p>A saved apparel size, custom print approval, perishable delivery cutoff and recurring box commitment create different requirements. The <a class="link" href="/for">store-type directory</a> helps choose which basket to demonstrate. For mixed catalogs, test the combined basket as well as each product type; a tool that handles one line correctly may lose the other line’s terms.</p>
<h2>Store guides</h2>
<p>{SEGMENTS.map(segment => <a class="link mr-4 inline-block mb-3" href={`/for/${segment.slug}`}>{segment.name}</a>)}</p>
<h2>Separate lifecycle jobs</h2>
<p>Cart recovery, browse follow-up, subscription servicing and post-purchase help should have explicit owners. An existing customer can qualify for several messages at once; decide which intent takes priority and inspect the queue after a purchase or support pause. Use the <a class="link" href="/use-cases">use-case directory</a> to investigate adjacent workflows.</p>
<h2>Use-case catalog</h2>
<p>{USE_CASES.map(useCase => <a class="link mr-4 inline-block mb-3" href={`/use-cases/${useCase.slug}`}>{useCase.name}</a>)}</p>
<h2>Compare total operating cost</h2>
<p>Request a quote for the same contact population, send volume, channels, support and migration scope. Include internal maintenance time and overlap with existing contracts. For incentives, subtract the discount from revenue before calculating contribution; do not discount only the gross-profit figure. Replace illustrative assumptions with store costs before deciding.</p>
<h2>Make a measurable decision</h2>
<p>Record the current workflow, candidate requirement, proposed rehearsal and rollback owner. Test a purchase exit, unavailable variant, missing permission and duplicate workflow before enabling a replacement. Then evaluate additional contribution over a defined observation window, including returns and channel costs. This site does not report firsthand tests or guarantee recovery results.</p>
<h2>Continue the research</h2>
<p>Open <a class="link" href="/apps">apps</a> for the directory, <a class="link" href="/compare">comparisons</a> for pairwise decisions, or <a class="link" href="/guides">decision guides</a> for timing, incentives and measurement. Linked pages remain individual research inputs, not site-wide quality certification.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
